            <ArticleTitle>Three-bundle popliteus tendon: a nonsymptomatic anatomical variation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>342-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 34-year-old man suffering from knee pain on the medial side of his right knee underwent knee arthroscopy. The arthroscopy revealed the popliteus tendon with an appearance of three bundles. Three-bundle popliteus tendon is a normal variant finding with no clinical significance.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
